    {
      "id": "p0105-b002",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "In general, Japanese words can be written with fewer characters than English words. This difference often requires English text to be abbreviated in Japanese-to-English game translations. Such abbreviation filled games were especially common in Japanese RPGs translated during the 1990s. Naturally, heavy text abbreviations can lead to confusion, unintentional laughs, or even complete loss of meaning.",
        "raw": "In general, Japanese words can be written with fewer characters\nthan English words. This difference often requires English text to be\nabbreviated in Japanese-to-English game translations. Such abbreviation\nfilled games were especially common in Japanese RPGs translated during\nthe 1990s. Naturally, heavy text abbreviations can lead to confusion,\nunintentional laughs, or even complete loss of meaning.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.11923938,
          0.11822143,
          0.67498588,
          0.21633571
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.11719901,
          0.11750714,
          0.67702626,
          0.21740714
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          2,
          3,
          4,
          5,
          6,
          7
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "一般来说，日语词汇所需的字符比英语少。因此，日本游戏译成英语时，经常不得不缩写英文。这种满是缩写的游戏，在20世纪90年代翻译的日本 RPG 中尤其常见。大量缩写自然可能造成困惑、无心的笑料，甚至让原意完全丢失。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
